## Phase 2 — v2.0 Beta: AI Coach + Study Coach + Gateway (Week 3)

### 2.1 API Gateway (:8080)
- [x] Spring Cloud Gateway project
- [x] [application.yml](file:///c:/Users/chira/Desktop/%E2%98%95%20Focus%20Flow/api-gateway/src/main/resources/application.yml) routing rules:
  - `/api/sessions/**` → `session-service:8081`
  - `/api/coach/**` → `coach-service:8082`
  - `/api/study/**` → `study-service:8083`
- [x] Global CORS configuration (allow all origins, methods, headers)

### 2.2 AI Coach Service (:8082)
- [x] Spring Boot project (stateless — no DB)
- [x] [ClaudeApiClient.java](file:///c:/Users/chira/Desktop/%E2%98%95%20Focus%20Flow/study-service/src/main/java/com/focusflow/study/client/ClaudeApiClient.java) — Java `HttpClient` wrapper for Anthropic REST API
  - Headers: `x-api-key`, `anthropic-version: 2023-06-01`, `Content-Type: application/json`
  - 60s timeout
- [x] [AiCoachService.java](file:///c:/Users/chira/Desktop/%E2%98%95%20Focus%20Flow/coach-service/src/main/java/com/focusflow/coach/service/AiCoachService.java) — fetch session summary from Session Service, call Claude, return insights
  - System prompt: warm coaching tone, data-driven insights (200–300 words)
  - Cache last response to avoid redundant API calls
- [x] [AiCoachController.java](file:///c:/Users/chira/Desktop/%E2%98%95%20Focus%20Flow/javafx-client/src/main/java/com/focusflowai/controller/AiCoachController.java) endpoints:
  - [x] `POST /api/coach/insights` — generate new coaching report
  - [x] `GET /api/coach/insights/latest` — return cached report (404 if none)
- [x] [application.yml](file:///c:/Users/chira/Desktop/%E2%98%95%20Focus%20Flow/api-gateway/src/main/resources/application.yml) with `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` and `SESSION_SERVICE_URL` env vars

### 2.3 Study Coach Service (:8083)
- [x] Spring Boot project with JPA + PostgreSQL + Gson
- [x] [Deck.java](file:///c:/Users/chira/Desktop/%E2%98%95%20Focus%20Flow/javafx-client/src/main/java/com/focusflowai/model/Deck.java) + [Flashcard.java](file:///c:/Users/chira/Desktop/%E2%98%95%20Focus%20Flow/javafx-client/src/main/java/com/focusflowai/model/Flashcard.java) JPA entities
- [x] PostgreSQL schema: `decks` + `flashcards` tables (FK cascade delete)
- [x] [StudyCoachService.java](file:///c:/Users/chira/Desktop/%E2%98%95%20Focus%20Flow/study-service/src/main/java/com/focusflow/study/service/StudyCoachService.java) — [generateDeck()](file:///c:/Users/chira/Desktop/%E2%98%95%20Focus%20Flow/study-service/src/main/java/com/focusflow/study/service/StudyCoachService.java#48-83):
  - Send source text to Claude with structured JSON prompt
  - Parse `{"cards":[{"question":"...","answer":"..."}]}` response
  - Persist deck + cards
- [x] [StudyController.java](file:///c:/Users/chira/Desktop/%E2%98%95%20Focus%20Flow/javafx-client/src/main/java/com/focusflowai/controller/StudyController.java) endpoints:
  - [x] `GET /api/study/decks` — list all decks
  - [x] `POST /api/study/decks/generate` — generate deck from source text via Claude
  - [x] `GET /api/study/decks/{id}/cards` — get cards for a deck
  - [x] `PATCH /api/study/cards/{id}/known` — update known status
  - [x] `DELETE /api/study/decks/{id}` — cascading delete

